# Wedge product

Canonical docs: `docs/product/overview.md`, `docs/product/roadmap.md`. Earlier phases are history in `docs/product/history/` and are not updated. Design spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-wedge-1.0-redesign-design.md`.

## What Wedge is

macOS **menu-bar only** app (no Dock, no Cmd-Tab). **Requires macOS 26 Tahoe**; no fallbacks for older systems. The bar shows **Now** (list index 0). Everything below is **Up Next**, in order. Position is priority: no priority fields, tags or multiple lists. **Done** is the one moment with motion and sound.

## Language

**Now** · **Up Next** · **Done** (title case as labels). Shortcut names: **Show Wedge** · **Done**. Menu: Done · Undo Done · Settings… · Quit Wedge.

Words to avoid: "one thing", OneThing, Focus, Spotlight (for Wedge's own concepts), Today, On Deck, Priority, Pinned, push, pop, stack, P0/P1. "Pop" is an internal name only; the UI says **Done sound** and **Pop (default)** for the bundled sound.

Voice: quiet and plain. No praise, no emoji, no exclamation marks, no OS-version caveats in UI copy. Every failure is a short inline message; never `NSSound.beep()`. Never compare Wedge to other apps in docs, UI or code.

Empty bar: the Wedge glyph (template image). Non-empty: the Now item's title only.

All UI strings come from the String Catalog through `WedgeCopy` (`wedge/Copy/WedgeCopy.swift`). Add new copy there, not as literals in views. Code names follow the UI noun (`NowHeader`).

## Behaviour rules

- **Panel:** borderless, non-activating glass panel anchored under the status item, 320 pt wide. Opens with the add field focused. Closes on ⌃⌥W, Esc (only when not editing) or click outside.
- **List:** Now is row 1 of the same list as Up Next. Dragging a row to the top makes it Now (no Done animation). Adds go to the bottom; the first item becomes Now. **Max 40 characters**; no truncation.
- **Edit:** click row text, or ↩ on a selected row. ↩ saves; Esc cancels the edit before it ever closes the panel; click elsewhere saves.
- **Done:** one `DoneAction` for every entry point (ring, ⌘↩, ⌥-click, menu, ⌃⌥D, the Mark Done intent). With the panel hidden: menu-bar swap, bump and sound only, and no undo hint later. Reduce Motion: instant swap plus sound.
- **Undo Done** (⌘Z, menu) restores the last Done item to the top until the next list mutation. Deletes are not undoable.
- **Keys:** ⌃⌥W Show Wedge and ⌃⌥D Done are the defaults, both remappable. In the panel: ↑/↓ select, ↩ edit, ⌘↩ Done, ⌫ delete, ⌥⌘↑/↓ move, ⌘Z undo, ⌘, Settings.
- **Errors:** save failure, damaged file (copy kept) and unreadable file each show a banner in the panel. After an unreadable file, saving stays off for the rest of the run so the file is never overwritten.
- **Settings:** one page. Menu Bar (Bold, Color), Done (Play sound, Sound, ≤ 3 s custom file), Keyboard, Open at login, About.
- **App Intents:** Add to Up Next, Mark Done, Get Now. Phrases: "Add to Up Next in Wedge", "Mark Done in Wedge", "What's Now in Wedge". Dependencies are registered in `AppDelegate.init`.
- **Privacy:** no analytics and no background network access. The only network call is the update check (Sparkle), which runs only when the user clicks Check for Updates, and only fetches the appcast and update from GitHub Releases; automatic checks stay off. The sandbox's only network entitlement is outgoing connections, for that check. The privacy manifest declares the UserDefaults and system-boot-time required-reason APIs and no data collection. Do not add a dependency or entitlement that changes this.
- **Storage:** `Application Support/Wedge/wedge.json` (versioned, atomic writes) inside the app's sandbox container. `UserDefaults` holds preferences only.

## Focused by default

Bug fixes, OS updates and polish ship freely. A new feature is added only by deliberate decision, with its own short design doc, and only if it fits the core rules: one item Now, order is priority, menu-bar only, local only.

Out of product (today's decisions): sync, iCloud, accounts, Dock mode, confetti, priority fields, tags or multiple lists, in-app updater, Mac App Store build, undo for anything but Done.

## Alignment

On any confirmed product change, update `docs/product/overview.md`, `docs/product/roadmap.md` and this rule together. Do not list a post-1.0 candidate until the decision and its design doc exist.
